From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 04:31:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/46] fix(gastown): stamp polecat_session on the work bead so
 the teardown liveness gate works (gcp-z2z)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Self-review of the previous commit found the live-owner gate was decorative.
polecat-worktree-reap.sh defers reaping while metadata.polecat_session names a
live session — the protection that keeps a PR-review polecat's worktree alive
through FIX_NEEDED rework, since the refinery closes the bead at PR creation.
But the startup claim block stamps polecat_session on the bead it claimed,
which under a formula-driven pool workflow is the STEP bead, not the work bead.
Checked live: work beads gcp-z2z and gcp-xbl carried work_dir, branch and
fork_sha but no polecat_session, so the gate would never have fired and rework
worktrees could be reclaimed mid-flight.

workspace-setup now writes polecat_session next to work_dir in the same
`gc bd update`, which is where the rest of the ownership metadata already
lands. Beads predating this stamp degrade safely rather than dangerously: with
no owner recorded the gate passes, the worktree is reaped only if it is also
closed and clean, and workspace-setup rebuilds it from metadata.branch on the
next run — wasteful, not lossy.

Also from self-review, both on the operator-facing signal, since the JSONL log
is the witness's only review surface for this teardown:
- A worktree whose `git status` fails was reported as `worktree_dirty_kept`
  ("uncommitted changes present"), conflating an unreadable checkout with a
  dirty one. It now reports `worktree_status_unreadable`, and the dirty case
  carries the actual count of uncommitted paths.
- `--dry-run` printed "reaped=N" for worktrees it had not touched; it now says
  "would reap=N (dry run)".

Test comment reworded to drop a `[bd ...]` bracket form that
tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py reads as an unrouted bare bd invocation.

Validation: shellcheck clean; go vet / golangci-lint / validate_registry /
go build / go test green; all four gastown shell suites pass. Both new
assertions mutation-checked — removing the polecat_session stamp fails the
contract test. The 7 failures in the CI pytest set (gascity claim-command,
discord/github intake service) reproduce identically on a pristine
origin/integration worktree and are filed as gcp-ks5.
---
 gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-worktree-reap.sh | 16 +++++++++++++---
 gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml          | 12 +++++++++++-
 gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml        |  1 +
 gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh       | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 gastown/tests/test_polecat_worktree_reap.sh     |  5 +++--
 5 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-worktree-reap.sh b/gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-worktree-reap.sh
index 5900cbf..340fd5d 100755
--- a/gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-worktree-reap.sh
+++ b/gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-worktree-reap.sh
@@ -213,9 +213,15 @@ while IFS= read -r WT; do
     # Gate 3: never discard uncommitted work. Ignored files are artifacts and
     # are excluded by `git status --porcelain`; untracked non-ignored files are
     # reported and block the reap so the witness can salvage them.
-    DIRTY=$(git -C "$WT" status --porcelain 2>/dev/null || printf 'UNREADABLE')
+    if ! DIRTY=$(git -C "$WT" status --porcelain 2>/dev/null); then
+        # A worktree git cannot even read is not one to delete on a guess.
+        record worktree_status_unreadable "$BEAD" "$WT" "git status failed in the worktree"
+        SKIPPED=$((SKIPPED + 1))
+        continue
+    fi
     if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
-        record worktree_dirty_kept "$BEAD" "$WT" "uncommitted changes present"
+        record worktree_dirty_kept "$BEAD" "$WT" \
+            "$(printf '%s\n' "$DIRTY" | wc -l | tr -d ' ') uncommitted path(s)"
         SKIPPED=$((SKIPPED + 1))
         continue
     fi
@@ -245,4 +251,8 @@ done <<EOF
 $CANDIDATES
 EOF
 
-echo "polecat-worktree-reap: reaped=$REAPED skipped=$SKIPPED (log: $LOG_FILE)"
+if [ "$DRY_RUN" -eq 1 ]; then
+    echo "polecat-worktree-reap: would reap=$REAPED skipped=$SKIPPED (dry run; log: $LOG_FILE)"
+else
+    echo "polecat-worktree-reap: reaped=$REAPED skipped=$SKIPPED (log: $LOG_FILE)"
+fi
diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
index 189a1ab..52b4d0d 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
@@ -107,9 +107,19 @@ cd "$WORKTREE_PATH"
 ```
 Record immediately so restarts and witness recovery can find it:
 ```bash
-gc bd update "$WORK_BEAD_ID" --set-metadata work_dir="$WORKTREE_PATH"
+gc bd update "$WORK_BEAD_ID" \
+  --set-metadata work_dir="$WORKTREE_PATH" \
+  --set-metadata polecat_session="${BEADS_ACTOR:-${GC_SESSION_NAME:-${GC_SESSION_ID:-${GC_AGENT:-}}}}"
 ```
 
+`polecat_session` must land on the WORK bead, not just on the step bead the
+startup claim block stamps. It is what tells the witness's
+`reap-merged-worktrees` teardown that you are still alive: on a PR-review rig
+the refinery closes this bead when the PR opens, while you stay available for
+FIX_NEEDED rework and still need this worktree. Without the stamp the witness
+sees no owner and may reclaim the directory out from under you — recoverable
+(workspace-setup rebuilds it from `metadata.branch`) but wasteful.
+
 Worktrees are scoped to the work bead (not the agent name) so that:
 - An agent can pick up new work even if an old worktree is being recovered
 - Multiple orphaned worktrees can coexist without collision
diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
index d3af93a..4098612 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
@@ -530,6 +530,7 @@ tail -n 50 "${LOG_DIR:-$GC_CITY/.gc/runtime/logs}/polecat-worktree-reap.log"
 | `worktree_dirty_kept` | Closed bead, uncommitted changes on disk | Salvage per Case C/D, then re-run |
 | `worktree_owner_live` | Closed bead, polecat still alive (PR rework) | None — expected; next cycle retries |
 | `worktree_bead_unreadable` | `gc bd show` returned nothing | If it persists, check Dolt health |
+| `worktree_status_unreadable` | `git status` failed inside the worktree | Inspect by hand; likely a broken or moved checkout |
 | `worktree_reap_failed` | Directory survived removal | Investigate permissions/mounts, mail mayor |
 
 A `worktree_dirty_kept` that repeats across cycles means real work is
diff --git a/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh b/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
index 58089e8..973236e 100755
--- a/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
+++ b/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
@@ -248,6 +248,22 @@ test_post_merge_worktree_teardown_has_an_owner() {
     grep -F 'Do NOT delete this worktree yourself' "$polecat" >/dev/null ||
         fail "polecat formula should point worktree teardown at the witness"
 
+    # The live-owner gate reads metadata.polecat_session off the WORK bead. The
+    # startup claim block only stamps the step bead, so without this write the
+    # gate is decorative and PR rework can lose its worktree.
+    grep -F -e '--set-metadata polecat_session="${BEADS_ACTOR:-${GC_SESSION_NAME:-${GC_SESSION_ID:-${GC_AGENT:-}}}}"' \
+        "$polecat" >/dev/null ||
+        fail "workspace-setup must stamp polecat_session on the work bead for the teardown liveness gate"
+    python3 - "$polecat" <<'PY' || fail "polecat_session must be stamped alongside work_dir, not somewhere unrelated"
+import sys
+text = open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8").read()
+start = text.index('**If no worktree** — create one scoped to the bead')
+end = text.index('**3. Ensure branch exists.**')
+block = text[start:end]
+if 'work_dir="$WORKTREE_PATH"' not in block or 'polecat_session=' not in block:
+    raise SystemExit(1)
+PY
+
     # The gates are the safety contract; losing any one of them silently turns
     # housekeeping into data loss.
     grep -F '*/polecats/*/worktrees/*' "$reaper" >/dev/null ||
diff --git a/gastown/tests/test_polecat_worktree_reap.sh b/gastown/tests/test_polecat_worktree_reap.sh
index 86b871c..7b72c70 100644
--- a/gastown/tests/test_polecat_worktree_reap.sh
+++ b/gastown/tests/test_polecat_worktree_reap.sh
@@ -14,8 +14,9 @@ write_gc_stub() {
     mkdir -p "$bin"
     cat >"$bin/gc" <<'SH'
 #!/usr/bin/env sh
-# Serves the two reads polecat-worktree-reap.sh performs:
-#   gc [bd --rig <rig>] show <bead> --json
+# Serves the two reads polecat-worktree-reap.sh performs, in both their
+# rig-scoped and unscoped forms:
+#   gc bd --rig <rig> show <bead> --json
 #   gc session list --state=all --json
 case "$1" in
     session)
-- 
